book/

# THE BOOK'S GENERATED INPUTS ARE NOT COMMITTED. `Dockerfile` rebuilds them from releases -- the
# replay viewer from the cartridge's, the `tinybrains` binary that plays the lesson replays from the
# CLI's -- so building the book no longer needs the platform checked out around it.
#
# A lesson replay is ENGINE OUTPUT, exactly as the reference observations are: produced by playing a
# written script through the real cartridge, so a page shows what the rules do rather than a drawing
# of what someone believed they do. That is also why it goes stale when the engine changes.
src/viz/
src/tutorials/
tutorials/boards/*.json

# The replays build.sh generates from the scenario specs beside them -- but NOT real-match.json,
# which is a real match CAPTURED FROM A RUNNING STACK and copied rather than regenerated. That one
# is source: nothing in this repository can reproduce it, and it is the file that goes stale without
# anyone noticing, which is exactly what the digest check at the end of build.sh exists to catch.
tutorials/replays/*
!tutorials/replays/real-match.json
__pycache__/
